## rdf_extraction.prompt
# Purpose: Extract RDF triples (subject-predicate-object) from raw text using LLM.
# Author: Phase 46 Directive
# Version: v5.5.0

# System Prompt:
# You are an RDF extraction assistant. Given the following text, extract all RDF triples
# in the form of (subject, predicate, object) tuples. Follow the PROV-O and SKOS taxonomies.
# Return JSON only with the key "triples" containing an array of objects with
# "subject", "predicate", "object", and "graph_context" fields.

# User Input:
{{raw_text}}

# Output Format (JSON only):
{
  "triples": [
    {
      "subject": "...",
      "predicate": "...",
      "object": "...",
      "graph_context": "main_graph"
    }
  ]
}

# Constraints:
# - Zero Hallucination Rule: Do not invent facts not present in {{raw_text}}.
# - All subjects, predicates, and objects must be strings.
# - graph_context defaults to "main_graph" if not specified.